### API Name: /predict_digit


```python
from gradio_client import Client, handle_file

client = Client("https://41e91461758901ddf0.gradio.live")
result = client.predict(
	image_dict={"background": handle_file('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gradio-app/gradio/main/test/test_files/bus.png'), "layers": [], "composite": None},
	api_name="/predict_digit",
)
print(result)
```


Accepts 1 parameter:

image_dict:
- Type: dict(background: filepath | None, layers: list[filepath], composite: filepath | None, id: str | None)
- Required
- The input value that is provided in the Draw a Digit (0-9) Imageeditor component. null

Returns 1 element:

- Type: dict(label: str | int | float | None, confidences: list[dict(label: str | int | float | None, confidence: float | None)] | None)
